{
  "dom_id": "question-344326",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+10y=f(x),\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=6\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x)$ is $4$-periodic and odd. Select the missing part in the solution of the BVP, where the infinite sum on the right-hand side below represents a particular solution ${y}_{p}$ of the differential equation.\n\n*Hint: In this specific problem, the forcing function $f(x)$ is chosen such that the particular solution ${y}_{p}$ satisfies ${y}_{p}^{′}(0)=0$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}(1)=0.$*\n\n$$\ny(x)∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
